WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.838
Time-based rules can change from day to day if they
use the

00:00:02.862 --> 00:00:07.325
current system date For teaching and grading that
can make results hard

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:13.888
to reproduce The source module therefore uses a
fixed reference date August 11, 2026

00:00:14.775 --> 00:00:18.175
The WHERE clause selects admissions from the
preceding thirty days and keeps

00:00:18.188 --> 00:00:23.888
Pneumonia or Flu diagnoses The CASE expression
identifies high-risk respiratory cases

00:00:23.912 --> 00:00:28.300
when the patient is at least sixty years old Other
respiratory cases

00:00:28.325 --> 00:00:33.762
receive a simpler label Run the query and inspect
the dates Because

00:00:33.788 --> 00:00:37.088
the reference date is fixed every student should get
the same result

00:00:37.112 --> 00:00:38.725
even when they run the lesson later
